Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:49:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] playstate: keep Transcode across a job gap of the same
 playback

Intent: ValidatePlayMethod turns a reported Transcode into DirectPlay
when no transcoding job carries the reported PlaySessionId. A web
stream change (burned-in subtitle, quality, audio track) or a seek
restart kills the running job before the next one registers at its
first segment, and the web client's throttled progress report in that
gap carries the killed job's PlaySessionId. The session then read
DirectPlay next to a live NVENC transcode until the next client report
(up to 10 s, replayed by the server's progress timer in between). The
downgrade now also requires that the reporting user's session on that
device is not already playing the same item as Transcode. A new item,
including the next track of a playlist, still gets upstream's check,
and a real switch to direct play reports DirectPlay itself.
PlaystateControllerTests covers the kept case and both downgrades; the
kept case fails against upstream.
Drop when: upstream tolerates the gap between a killed and a restarted
transcode, or the web client stops reporting with the killed job's
PlaySessionId.

Patch: 0025
